Bugfix: Keep the file row action buttons in their own box

The share and menu buttons of a file row were 16px tall while their icons sat
18px lower, so the keyboard focus ring framed empty space above the icon. The
action block also dropped below the file name in the file list and in both
sharing lists, and covered the row underneath.

The buttons now keep the height of the line they sit in, and the action block
returns to the right edge of the name cell. In the incoming shares list, where
the actions carry text, the row distributes name and actions one level up so
that a long file name no longer runs under them. The focus ring frames the
button a keyboard user is on.

WCAG 2.1 AA, SC 2.4.7
